ge>A68</fpage><lpage>71</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2069680</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002732-Chang1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>HC</given-names></name><name><surname>Doerge</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Dietary genistein inactivates rat thyroid peroxidase in vivo without an apparent hypothyroid effect.</article-title><source>Toxicol Appl Pharmacol</source><volume>168</volume><fpage>244</fpage><lpage>252</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11042097</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002732-Okura1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Okura</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Arakawa</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Oka</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Yoshinari</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Monden</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><year>1988</year><article-title>Effect of genistein on topoisomerase activity and on the growth of &#x0005b;Val 12&#x0005d;Ha-ras-transformed NIH 3T3 cells.</article-title><source>Biochem Biophys Res Commun</source><volume>157</volume><fpage>183</fpage><lpage>189</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2848517</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002732-Markovits1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Markovits</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Linassier</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Fosse</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Couprie</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Pierre</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1989</year><article-title>Inhibitory effects of